<!--
  This file records a subset of the ApiCompat breaks in Azure.ResourceManager.ProviderHub 1.3.0:
  the ones that come from regenerating the package on the current management-plane generator rather
  than from the upstream compliance change to the Microsoft.ProviderHub specification.

  Measured against the 1.2.1 baseline, the regeneration produces 97 distinct ApiCompat findings.
  Only 26 of them name an internal-only Microsoft identifier removed by the compliance change; the
  remaining 71 name nothing sensitive. ApiCompat suppression targets are fully qualified signatures
  and the tool supports no wildcard, so suppressing those 26 would reproduce in this repository the
  exact identifiers the upstream change exists to remove. They are described by location and shape
  in the package CHANGELOG.md instead.

  Four findings that were previously listed here have since been fixed rather than suppressed, by
  restoring the members in src/Custom: the synchronous ProviderRegistrationResource.Delete pair and
  the flattened ResourceTypeRegistrationResourceManagementOptions.BatchProvisioningSupportSupported-
  Operations property.

  NOTE: this file is currently not consumed by the build. ApiCompat is gated on a non-empty
  <ApiCompatVersion> in the project file (see eng/Directory.Build.Common.targets), which is absent
  for this package, and Azure.ResourceManager.ProviderHub is listed in ApiCompatVersionOptOut.txt.
  The entries below are therefore a record for reviewers, not active suppressions.
-->
